Goal:- lab has an admin panel at /admin. It's only accessible to logged-in users with a roleid of 2. Solve the lab by accessing the admin panel and using it to delete the user carlos. 

Observation:- While changing the email address , role id was disclosed inside JSON

Steps to solve :- 

        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Login using the given credentials
        Step3:- change the email and capture the request in burpsuit 
        step4:- send the request to repeater check the JSON
        Step5:- Role id, email , api was disclosed inside JSON as 


{
  "username": "wiener",
  "email": "xyz@gmail.com",
  "apikey": "JIsIg0ZUTQbPFgx8HPnxuxhZHSTYw9fehwUv",
  "roleid": 1
}


        Step6:- change role id to 2 
        Step7:- You got the access to admin pannel 
        Step8:- Delete user carlos

Result:- Access to admin pannel and we can add or delete user from the database

Root Cause:- Sensitive parameter roleid was exposed and modifiable through client-side JSON without server-side validation.

Fix:- Enforce server-side authorization, restrict editable parameters, and prevent users from modifying role-related fields.
